# Housing Guide UK — environment configuration
#
# This project is a plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript site with no build step, so the
# browser cannot read a .env file directly. This file exists to document the
# two values you need from Supabase. To actually use them locally, copy
# js/config.example.js to js/config.js and paste the same two values in
# there (see README.md "Local development" for the full walkthrough).
#
# Where to find these values:
# Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API

# The URL of your Supabase project.
# Safe to expose in frontend code — it is just an address, not a secret.
SUPABASE_URL=

# The public "anon" key for your Supabase project.
# Safe to expose in frontend code. This key can only do what your Row Level
# Security (RLS) policies in database/policies.sql explicitly allow.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER put a service_role key, database password, or any other secret here
# or anywhere in frontend code. The service_role key bypasses Row Level
# Security completely. This project never needs it in the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
